{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to be1a840a, CE-2: the absence proof needs scope evidence.\nThe second choice.\n\n`absent` is a terminal fact. An agent that reads it can send the\nsame work again under a new key. So the fact must not rest on a\nbound between two clocks that the contract does not state.\n\nPredicate. The proof passes only when all of these hold.\n1. The latest signing is dead by `Custody.dead`, as today. This\n   check stays the precondition of `absent`. It is no part of the\n   proof.\n2. The journal is continuous from genesis through the fixed head,\n   and it holds no entry of this actor with this idempotency key.\n3. The time that the verified journal gives for the fixed head is\n   at or past the `notAfter` of that signing.\n\nWhy item 3 is enough. The judge refuses an intent as `expired` when\nthe commit clock is at or past `notAfter` (`judge.ts` line 301). A\nrecorded act with a clock behind the previous entry's time gets\n`clock-behind` and no entry (`judge.ts` line 495). So each later\ncommit judges at or past the head's time, and it refuses this\nenvelope. Confirm that for each path that admits a signed act. If\none path judges below the sealed time, stop and send it to me.\n\nUnsupported evidence. When the head's time is before `notAfter`,\nthe proof fails. The record stays as it is, the call sends nothing,\nand the answer gives a reason of its own: the scope's record shows\nno time at or past the expiry of this request. The `next` text says\nto settle again after the scope records a later entry. This reason\njoins the list of item 2 of ruling d264dea5.\n\nTake the time from the verified journal, not from an unverified\nsummary. Add no clock field and no time route. Do not read the\nhead's time as the current time of the scope.\n\nThe note states three facts.\n- A slow scope clock keeps the record open, and no margin decides\n  the ending.\n- A store that is full of dead records toward a quiet scope does\n  not recover by `settle` alone. An entry of any signer after the\n  expiry opens the way, and so does the card check, which gets a\n  Native answer to the same envelope.\n- The 60-second margin still decides when a caller may ask.\n\nWitness of item 5 of d264dea5, with two changes. The scripted log\ngets one entry of another signer, at or past the expiry, before the\nrecovery. One paired control: with the head's time 1 ms before\n`notAfter` the proof fails with the new reason and admission stays\nfull, and with the head's time equal to `notAfter` it passes.\n\nThe card route of bc7d46d5 does not change. The wire shapes, the\nbounds and the queue do not change. CE-2 stays after RS-1.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}